			<div class="content" id="post-content-4556074">
									

<p>The self-title it proclaims reminds me a lot of some of the tales involving <a href="/scp-3388">Carnegias/Poky</a>; that would be a rather fun interaction with this thing.</p>
<p>I enjoy this, but the logs do feel kinda <em>off</em>; the last few lines, for example:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p><strong>SCP-5954:</strong> Even the most basic of fundamentals in carriership, someone didn’t know how to water a peace lily, poor thing was dry to the bone!<br />
<strong>Elliot:</strong> … So, you’re saying these plants were causing you psychic pain?<br />
<strong>SCP-5954:</strong> How they cried! Day and night! It was an unending tragedy as they faded with the dreadful lamentations unto the coil of death.<br />
<strong>Elliot:</strong> That… we can work with that.</p>
</blockquote>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>I don't feel like these two are actually having the same conversation. The SCP already mentioned feeling the pain of nearby plants in the previous log, presumably a short time ago, but Elliot acts like this is the first she's hearing of it. Plus, the SCP didn't actually mention pain here when Elliot realizes it. And then SCP-5954 says something that isn't really a clear answer to her question, followed by Elliot saying something that also doesn't look like a response to what it just said about plant cries.</p>

